	abstract = {When researching Tribal law, which includes statutes, court cases, orders, and rules, it is important to focus on the importance of looking at non-legal information to gain context of the tribe's culture. This chapter provides recommendations for legal researchers, especially law librarians, who may be supporting tribal legal research on best practices to address the challenges of conducting tribal legal research. The challenges to conducting tribal legal research include access to tribal law and complications of the increasing use of AI in legal research. Key issues for consideration when using AI include the bias of AI, its limited training data, and how the attainment of this data may threaten a tribe's sovereignty. This chapter offers best practices to address those challenges by centering the concept of Indigenous Data Sovereignty and offering a research process that incorporates the unique considerations when researching tribal law. © 2025 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.},
