	doi = {10.1016/j.epsr.2024.111403},
	abstract = {With the rapid advancement of artificial intelligence (AI) technology, particularly the successful application of large models across various fields, the energy industry is experiencing a new wave of technological innovation. Virtual power plants (VPPs), which integrate distributed energy resources (DERs) as an innovative power system management model, face challenges such as optimal dispatching, market participation, and system security. This paper examines the research progress of AI large models in the energy sector, exploring their current applications, technical limitations, and future development directions in VPPs. By analyzing the core characteristics of large model technology and its specific applications in VPP operations, market strategy formulation, data management, and user interaction, the study highlights the multifaceted value that large models add to VPPs. The findings show that large models significantly improve operational efficiency, system security, and user services in VPPs, yet they encounter technical and managerial challenges like data security, model transparency, and system integration. Consequently, this paper proposes strategies and recommendations to overcome these challenges, promoting the deep integration and sustainable development of large model technology in VPPs. AI large models are poised to drive intelligent and digital power systems, fostering technological innovation, enhancing power system efficiency, and achieving sustainable energy goals. © 2024 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.},
	language = {English},
