	abstract = {The increasing deployment of Automated Vehicles (AVs) necessitates effective Explainable Artificial Intelligence (XAI) models to enhance user trust through transparent decision-making. While these models employ diverse techniques, they often prioritize algorithmic interpretability over human cognitive and linguistic processes. This paper introduces PsyLingXAV, a framework that integrates psycholinguistic principles into AV explanations, leveraging the psychology of language to optimize communication with users. By grounding explanation design in cognitively and linguistically informed strategies, PsyLingXAV tailors outputs to the driving context, advancing AV explainability. This work paves the way for more intuitive, human-centered explanations in AVs, with future studies poised to validate its impact. © 2025 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.},
